<title>USA: Worldcom Q1 shr profit vs pro forma loss.</title>
<headline>Worldcom Q1 shr profit vs pro forma loss.</headline>
<dateline>JACKSON, Miss. 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>FIRST QUARTER</p>
<p>				 ACTUAL	     PRO FORMA</p>
<p>				 1997		   1996</p>
<p>					   % of	% of</p>
<p>			  Amount  Revenue   Amount  Revenue  Change</p>
<p> Revenue		  $1,677.2  100.0% $1,243.8  100.0%   35%</p>
<p> EBITDA			393.4  23.5%     261.2  21.0%    51%</p>
<p> Operating income	  170.5  10.2%	54.3   4.4%   214%</p>
<p>Earnings Per Share (EPS)</p>
<p>				  0.05     --    (0.10)     --     --</p>
<p> Cash earnings(A)	   0.20     --	0.06     --   233%</p>
<p>NOTE: Pro forma numbers show results as if WorldCom had merged with MFS Communications Co and UUNet Technologies Inc a year ago. WorldComm merged with the two companies in December.</p>
<p>The 1997 first quarter results include MFS goodwill amortization of $84 million.  Under purchase accounting treatment of the MFS merger, 1996 results are not similarly impacted.</p>
<p>(A) Adding back MFS purchase accounting amortization ($0.09) and cash utilization of MFS tax loss carry forwards ($0.06).</p>
<p>Primary earnings per share were $0.05 for the three months ended March 31, 1997 and $0.22 for the 1996 period. Fully diluted EPS was $0.05 for the 1997 period vs $0.21 for the 1996 period.</p>
<p>Full Company name WorldCom Inc.</p>
</text>
